<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_{"></a><b>3-2-1 Transformation</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command 3-2-1 allows the user to construct transformation from a plane, line,and point.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_A"></a><b>Activate for Scanning</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">If Activate for Scanning command is enabled all new scans and captured data will pass&nbsp; through the activated transformation, their co-ordinates will not be in the global&nbsp; space.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Align Entities</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Align Entities command uses best fit algorithm to move one entity in spaceso toget maximum overlapping of the reference entity and entity moved.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Align to Plane</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Align View command aligns view direction orthogonal to the selected datum plane orplane reducible datum entity (cylinder, circle, cone, slots).<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Align View</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Align View command aligns view direction orthogonal to the datum plane.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Annotation</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Short note inserted to an inspection page in Inspection mode<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Apply</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command Apply launches the Transformation Apply mode.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Apply Reverse</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Apply Reverse command transforms visible selected entities by applying the reversedtransformation matrix.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Apply to Selection</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Apply to Selection command transforms visible selected entities from the global co-ordinatesystem to the co-ordinate system defined by the marked transformation.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Area 2D Sampling</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Area Sampling command samples the visible selected scan data patch by patch. It works on entire entity, no matter if the scans are selected wholly or partially<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Auto Extract Circle</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Auto Extract Circle command fits and creates datum circles to the visible mesh selections.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Auto Extract Cone</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Auto Extract Cone command fits and creates datum cones to the visible mesh selections.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Auto Extract Cylinder</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Auto Extract Cylinder command fits and creates datum cylinders to the visible meshselections.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Auto Extract Plane</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Auto Extract Plane command fits and creates datum planes to the visible mesh selections.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Auto Extract Rectangular Slot</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Auto Extract Rectangular Slot command fits and creates datum rectangular slots tothe visible mesh selections.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Auto Extract Round Slot</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Auto Extract Round Slot command fits and creates datum round slots to the visiblemesh selections.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Auto Extract Sphere</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Auto Extract Sphere command fits and creates datum spheres to the visible mesh selections.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Average Noise Reduction</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Average Noise Reduction command reduces noise in the visible selected data byapplying an average (Laplacian) filter.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_B"></a><b>Back</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Back command to set the viewport orthogonal to OXY plane from -Z side.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Back to World CS</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Back to World CS command restores the World CS as current CS and applies all non-lockedentities to it.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Batch</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Batch command carries out a series of mesh functions automatically.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Bind Views</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When enabled Bind Views - Absolute will cause all open windows to display the same visible region and to update all views simultaneously according to the active window.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_C"></a><b>Cap</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Cap command caps selected mesh holes.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Chordal Tolerancing</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Chordal Tolerancing command is the process of following a line and representing itby a polyline with the minimum number of points that will not deviate from the originalline by more than the defined error tolerance.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Clear</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Clear command restores the World CS as current CS without applying the non-lockedentities to it<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Combine</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command Combine is used to join two transformation matrices in a single one.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Combine Selected Entities</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Combine Selected Entities command combines all visible selected entities of one typeinto single entity of the same type.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Copy</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Copy command copies the visible selection and places it in the clipboard.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Copy as Transformation</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Copy as Transformation command creates a copy of Current CS in Transformations group.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Create from Probe Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Create From Probe Points command creates a polyline from a sequence of visible selectedprobe points.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Create New Entity from Selection</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Create New Entity From Selection removes the visible selection and generates a copyof it as separate entity.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Create Polyline (Manual)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Create Polyline (Manual) command allows you to create a new polyline by manuallyselecting points on the visible data.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Create Viewport Entity</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command creates an entity, which stores the current viewport orientation.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Cut</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Cut command deletes the visible selection and places it in the clipboard.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Cut (Polygonal Area)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Cut (Polygonal Area) command deletes selected mesh triangles that fall into a drawnpolygon or selected plane and generates a new hidden mesh entity from them.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_D"></a><b>Deactivate</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command cancels the scanning and capturing through active transformation.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Define XY Grid</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Define XY Grid command generates point cloud from mesh or scan data selection.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Delete command deletes the visible selection.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete All Dimensions</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command deletes all dimensions in the scene no matter if their entities arevisible or hidden.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete All Gap and Flush</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command deletes all Gap and FLush dimensions in the scene no matter if theirentities are visible or hidden.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete All Labels</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command deletes all labels in the scene no matter if their entities are visibleor hidden.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete Dimension</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command deletes the current dimension.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete Gap and Flush</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command deletes the current Gap and Flush dimension.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete Label</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command deletes the current labels.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Delete Selected</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Delete Selected command deletes marked entities/groups that are selected wholly orpartially.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Dimensioning</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command switches the mode for creating and editing dimensions.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Boundaries</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command affects the visual representation of all meshes in the scene. When thisoption is activated, KUBE draws mesh boundaries as connected lines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Grid</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Display Grid to show grid lines in views that are orthogonal to the global co-ordinatesystem.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Intensity</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Display Intensity displays the Intensity view for ModelMaker D sensor.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Laser Button</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Display Laser Button hides/shows the button for switching the laser on and off.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Localiser Position</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Display Localiser Position hides/shows the Localiser Position window.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Normals</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Display Normals to show objects point normals as short yellow lines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Sensor</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Display Sensor hides/shows the sensor view window, which is located in Scan Panebelow the localiser driven menu and localiser position window.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display Toolbar</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Enable/disable Toolbar option to show/hide the main toolbar in the KUBE application.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Display WorkSpace</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Display WorkSpace command hides/shows the workspace window that contain Entitiespane, and Output pane.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Down</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Down command to set the viewport orthogonal to OXZ plane from -Y side.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Draw First Point</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Draw First Point is available for polylines only. If you enable it, the first nodeof every polyline will be visualised as yellow filled square.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Draw Polyline Nodes as Crosses</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When you select Draw Polyline Nodes as Crosses,all nodes of every polyline will be visualised as yellow crosses oriented to thepolyline direction.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Draw Polyline Nodes as None</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">raw Polyline Nodes as None is available for polylines only. When you select it, nonodes will be displayed.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Draw Polyline Nodes as Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Draw Polyline Nodes as Points is available for polylines only. When you select it,all nodes of every polyline will be visualised as small yellow points.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Draw Polyline Nodes as Squares</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Draw Polyline Nodes as Squares is available for polylines only. When you select it,all nodes of every polyline will be visualised as outlined yellow squares orientedto the polyline direction.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_E"></a><b>Enable Undo</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Enable Undo command switches On/Off the Undo command.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Enhance Features</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Enhance Features command detects edges of the visible mesh selection and sharpenthem by pulling vertices towards the feature lines. You have three levels of controlhow strong the sharpness to be.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Exit</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Exits the KUBE. If there are opened and unsaved files, you will be asked whetherto save them or not.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Export</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The Export command converts data from the current document to different file formats.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Extract from Boundaries</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Extract From Boundaries command creates a polylines from visible selected mesh boundaries.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_F"></a><b>Fetch</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The Fetch command restores a previous state of data in the scene. It works as \"multiplesteps\" Undo command, but performed at once. The command is grayed when there is nosaved file state. You cannot Fetch File operations and operations in Inspection mode.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fill</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fill command reconstructs missing data (holes) in selected areas of the mesh.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Circle</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Circle command fits a datum circle to the visible selection, which may includescan data, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Cone</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Cone command fits a datum cone to the visible selection, which may include scandata, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Cylinder</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Cylinder command fits a datum cylinder to the visible selection, which may includescan data, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Line</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Line command fits a datum line to the visible selection, which may include scandata, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Multiple Lines</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Multiple Lines command fits a line through each stripe in the visible selectedscan data and calculates statistics.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Parallel Planes</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Parallel Planes (Manual) command fits a plane to the visible selection and asecond plane to all the visible unselected data.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Plane</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Plane command fits a datum plane to the visible selection, which may includescan data, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Point</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Point command fits a datum point to the visible selection, which may includescan data, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Fit Sphere</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Fit Sphere command fits a datum sphere to the visible selection, which may includescan data, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Flip Normals</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Flip Normals command inverts the normals of all selected and visible polygons. Thismeans that if an object is convex, after the operation it will be concave, andvice versa.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Format (Label)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command formats individual label.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>From 3 Entities</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command From 3 Entities allows the user to create interactively transformationmatrices using different definition methods.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>From N Constrained Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command is used to set up transformation by more than 3 correspondences or when no exact entity match is present and needed to set correspondencesby some of the co-ordinates only.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>From N Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Transformation From N Points command creates a transformation constructed from aset of known points.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>From Single Plane</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command From Single Plane allows the user to establish correspondence betweenan existing datum plane and one of the co-ordinate system planes.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>From Viewport</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command From Viewport allows the user to define correspondence between the realposition and the viewport position of an object in the scene.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Front</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Front command to set the viewport orthogonal to OXY plane from +Z side.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Front-Facing Mode Selection</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When this mode is enabled, all shape selections will select only the scan data andmesh triangles, which normals face front towards the viewport.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_G"></a><b>Gap and Flush</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command switches the mode for creating Gap and Flush dimensions.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_H"></a><b>Hide All</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Hide All hides marked entities and groups.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Hide Selection and Hide Selected</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Hide Selection hides all entities in the scene (or those parts of them) that areselected.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>History</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command History is used to manage the applied transformations to the currentCS.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Hold</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The Hold command saves the current state of the scene in a temporary file with .hff(Hold Fetch File) extension in the user's temporary folder<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_I"></a><b>Import Transformation</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Import Transformation allows you to import co-ordinate systems from other software.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Import XY Grid</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Import XY Grid command imports point cloud from *.txt, *asc, or *.csv file formats.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Instant Editing</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Instant Editing command applies different processing tools on meshes to areas definedin the dialog.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Interactive Cross Sections</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Interactive Cross Section command produces single polylines using a line definedinteractively using the mouse and the current view.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Interactive Noise Reduction by Curvature</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Interactive Noise Reduction By Curvature command modifies the visible selection basedon the local surrounding data and local curvature.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Interactive Transformation</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The command Interactive allows the user to create interactively transformation matricesusing different definition methods.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Inverse</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Inverse command inverses the transformation matrix of a transformation.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Invert Normals</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Invert Normals command flips the normals of a scan entity.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Invert Selection</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Invert Selection selects all visible unselected entities (or parts of them) and deselectsall visible selected entities (or parts of them).<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Isometric</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Isometric command to set the viewport from 45 degrees on all three axes: +X,+Y, and -Z.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_J"></a><b>Join</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Join command merges two visible polylines into a single one by connecting the endpoints of both polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_L"></a><b>Labeling</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command switches the mode for creating and editing labels for datums and pointsof compound entities.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Left</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Left command to set the viewport orthogonal to OYZ plane from -X side.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Light Adjust</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Light Adjust allows user to change the light direction in the scene.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Light Reset</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Default light direction can be restored using Light Reset command.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Linear [1D] Sampling</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Linear Sampling command modifies the visible selected scan data by re-sampling thestripes at a specified interval.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Lock in Space</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Lock in Space command locks single or multiple entities or groups so that they won'tbe affected when updating the Current CS.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_M"></a><b>Macro SpeedBar</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Show Macro SpeedBar command displays or hides the Macro SpeedBar dialog.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Material Colour</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Material Colour command is used for changing colours of the objects and is availablefor all entities and groups that have visual representation in the scene.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Material Reset</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Material Reset command is used for setting the default colours of the objects andis available for all entities and groups that have visual representation in the scene.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Median Noise Reduction</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Median Noise Reduction command reduces noise by applying a median filter on eachstripe or visible selected polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Merge</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Merge command creates a single polygon mesh from visible and selected scan data andmesh entities.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Modify (Current CS)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Modify (Current CS) command translates and rotates the current CS.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Modify (Dimension)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command formats individual dimension.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Modify (Transformation)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Modify command translates and rotates a transformation.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Modify Radius</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Modify Radius command increases/decreases radius of a datum sphere or circle.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_N"></a><b>New</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New is a standard Windows command to create new file.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Circle</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Circle command creates new datum circle.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Cone</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Cone command creates new datum cone.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Cylinder</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Cylinder command creates new datum cylinder.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Line</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Line command creates new datum line.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Plane</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Plane command creates new datum plane.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Point</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Point command creates new datum point.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Rectangular Slot</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Rectangular Slot command creates new datum rectangular slot.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Round Slot</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Round Slot command creates new datum round slot.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>New Sphere</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">New Sphere command creates new datum sphere.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Next CS</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Next CS command activates the next transformation in the history stack as currentCS.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Noise Reduction by Curvature</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Noise Reduction By Curvature command modifies the visible selection based on thelocal surrounding data and local curvature.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_O"></a><b>Offset</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Offset command translates a datum plane along its normal.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Offset Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Offset Points command is applied to scan data and meshes only.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>On Rotate/Pan Display ...</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">On Rotate/Pan Display... command affects visualisation of scan data, meshes,and point clouds in the scene during rotate, pan, and zoom actions and is related to the details of objects.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>On Rotate/Pan Draw ...</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">On Rotate/Pan Draw... command affects visualisation of scan data and meshes in&nbsp; the scene during rotate, pan, and zoom actions and is related to the appearance of&nbsp; objects.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Open</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Open is a standard Windows command to open an existing file.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Open in Current Document</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Open in current document is same as the Open command with one difference - it loadsthe file it in a currently active document.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Optimise Meshes</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Optimise Meshes command reduces the noise in mesh data by aligning patches.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Optimise Scan</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Optimise Scan command reduces the noise in scan data by aligning patches.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_P"></a><b>Pan</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When this mode is enabled, hold down the left mouse button and move the mouse onscreen. This will translate the viewport left, right, up, and down.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Parallel Cross Sections</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Parallel Cross Sections command creates a number of parallel cross sections throughthe visible selection.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Paste As New Entity</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Paste As New Entity command moves the data from the clipboard into the active document.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>PC Diagnostics</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The PC Diagnostics command is destined to check the specification of your PC againstthe requirements of KUBE.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Pick Feature Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Pick Feature Points command activates capturing of feature points, which is the firststep of the registration process.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Pick Pair of Planes</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The function Pick Pair of Planes is used to measure the on-screen distances and anglebetween planes.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Pick Pair of Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The function Pick Pair of Points is used to measure the on-screen distances betweenpoints.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Pick Selection</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When Pick Selection mode is selected, press on the toolbar button to activate it.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Pick Single Point</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command returns information about the currently picked point on a visible entity.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Play</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Play command displays an animated rotated view of the visible entities in the currentdocument.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Point Curvature</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Point curvature is a property of the mesh entities. The curvature at a given pointis determined by finding the greatest angle between the normals of the current vertexand the vertices from the chosen neighbourhood level<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Polygon Reduction</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Polygon Reduction command reduces points in the visible selected meshes.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Preferences</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call the command Preferences to change different KUBE settings.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Previous CS</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Previous CS command activates the previous transformation in the history stack ascurrent CS.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Properties</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Properties command calls the properties dialog for an entity, group or root.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Put Label</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command automatically creates label for each marked datum entity.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_R"></a><b>Radial Cross Sections</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Radial Cross Sections command creates a number of radial cross sections through thevisible selection.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Register</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Register command aligns two different surfaces in such a way so their common areascoincide. It works with scan data. mesh and point clouds entities.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Remove Duplicate Triangles</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Remove Duplicate Triangles command finds any visible selected triangles that haveidentical vertices in the mesh and removes the surplus triangles even if the directionsof their normals are opposite.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Remove Faulty Areas</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Remove Faulty Areas command removes visible selected triangles, which distort theimage.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Remove Floating Meshes</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Remove Floating Meshes command removes regions of the visible selected object, whichare isolated from the main mesh.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Remove Label</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command automatically removes label from each marked datum entity.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Rename</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Rename command renames single entity or group.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Rendering Mode</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">These context menu commands affect visual representation of scan data and meshes only.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Reorganise</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Reorganise command rearranges edges of the visible selections to follow detectionfeature lines (e.g. corners).<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Repair</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Repair command is a combination of two functions: Remove Faulty Areas and Fill afterwardsusing their default parameters.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Reset Software Settings</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Reset Software Settings command rolls back all settings to their initial values<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Reverse</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Reverse command reverses the direction of a datum line or the cylinder axe. Reverse command reverses direction of the normal of a datum plane or datum circle.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Reverse Order</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Reverse Order command reverses the direction of the visible selected polylines.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Right</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Right command to set the viewport orthogonal to OYZ plane from +X side.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Rotate</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When this mode is enabled and you hold down the left mouse button on the viewable&nbsp; area, a dashed circle will appear. If mouse pointer is within this circle, the viewpoint&nbsp; rotation is on all three axes; otherwise it is clockwise or counter-clockwise towards&nbsp; the viewport.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Rotate and Translate</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Rotate and Translate command offers possibility for manual adjustment of entity position.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Rotate Viewport</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Using Rotate Viewport an object can be rotated by an exact entry of degree arounda specified axis.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_S"></a><b>Sample Every</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Sample Every command samples the visible selected polylines at the given spacing.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Save (As)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Save is a standard Windows command to save the current file.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Scale Points</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Scale Points is applied to scan data, meshes, point clouds, probe points, and polylines.It scales the selection in X, Y, and/or Z directions of the local co-ordinate system.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select command selects marked entities/groups.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select All</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select All command selects all visible entities in the scene, no matter if thereare some wholly or partially selected entities.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select Boundaries</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select Boundaries command selects boundary triangles of visible scans and meshes.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select Box</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select Box command selects these visible points that are located in a specific boxdefined by minimum and maximum co-ordinates in X, Y, and Z.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select by Curvature</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select By Curvature computes the curvature per visible point comparing it's normaland it's neighbour's normal, decides whether it is a curved or a flat surface andselects it.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select by Point Normal</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select By Point Normal selects part of a visible scan based on the angle atwhich the points were scanned.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select by Type</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select By Type command selects all visible entities of the chosen type.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select None</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select None command unselects all visible entities in the scene, no matter if thereare some wholly or partially unselected entities.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select Polylines by Number of Nodes</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select Polylines by Number of Nodes command selects all visible polylines in thescene, which number of vertices (nodes) is less than the value set in the dialog.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select Reverse Scans</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select Reverse Scans selects parts of a visible scan captured while scanningin reverse direction.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select Thin Triangles</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select Thin Triangles command selects areas of visible scans and meshes containing&nbsp; triangles having an angle smaller than the given value.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select Triangles Based on Edge Length</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select Triangles Based On Edge Length command selects visible triangles based onthe length of their sides.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Select Triangles Based on Order</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Select Triangles Based on Order command selects part of a visible scan based on theorder in which the points were captured.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Selection (Polygonal, Free hand, Elliptic, Rectangular)</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The selection will consist of all visible points and whole visible entities thatare inside.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Set to Current View</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command changes the viewport orientation to the current one.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Show All</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Show All command displays all hidden entities (or those parts of them that are hidden.)<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Smooth Boundaries</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Smooth Boundaries command smoothes boundaries of the visible selections by creatingmore triangles.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Snapshot</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Snapshot captures the whole viewport.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Sort by Name</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Sort by Name command sorts all datum entities in the Datuming group by name.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Sort by Type</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Sort by Type command sorts all datum entities in the Datuming group by type.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Sort Polylines</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Sort Polylines command re-orders visible selected polylines so that their order reflectstheir position in space rather than the sequence in which they were created.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Split Mesh</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">The Split Mesh command divides the whole mesh entity to sub-meshes and creates Nnew mesh items in the entity tree.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Split Scan Data</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Split Scan Data command splits visible selected (wholly or partially) scan data entitiesinto entities containing single patches.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Static View</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Static View command affects visualisation of scan data (all rendering modes) andmeshes (when in Points or Large Points mode only) in a static scene and is relatedto the details of objects.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Stitch</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Stitch command attempts to fill the visible selected gaps in the mesh, by joiningthe boundaries of long thin holes.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Subdivide</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Subdivide command subdivides larger triangles within the visible selected area intosmaller ones.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_T"></a><b>Toggle Wireframe</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">These command toggles the current shading mode (Flat or Smooth) with shading + wireframemode (Flat + Wireframe or Smooth + Wireframe) and vice versa.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Trim Patches</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Trim Patches command removes the overlapping points on scan data patches at givenoverlapping distance. It works on entire entity, no matter if the scans are selectedwholly or partially.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Type In Transformation</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Type-In Transformation command is used to directly set rotation/translation valuesor the transformation matrix.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_U"></a><b>Undo</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Undo command restores the previous state of data in the scene. It works one stepback only.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Unify Normals</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Unify Normals command unifies all the polygon normals in the visible selected mesh.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Unify Normals Interactive</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Unify Normals Interactive command detects a submesh and inverts the normals whenclicking on a triangle with reverse normal .<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Unlock</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Unlock command unlocks single or multiple entities or groups so that they will beaffected when updating the current CS.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Unselect All</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Unselect All command unselects marked entities/groups that are selected (or partiallyselected).<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Up</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Call Up command to set the viewport orthogonal to OXZ plane from +Y side.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Update Current CS</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Update Current command updates the current co-ordinate system with the selected transformation.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Use View Position</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">This command applies a custom view position to the scene.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_V"></a><b>Volume [3D] Sampling</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Volume Sampling command fits a cubic grid to the visible selected mesh/scan data extents.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_W"></a><b>Weld</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Weld command removes surplus triangles.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><a name="bm_Z"></a><b>Zoom All</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Zoom All command resets the view extents to fit all visible data.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Zoom In</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Zoom In command magnifies all visible data twice.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Zoom Mode</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When this mode is enabled, hold down the left mouse button and move the mouse upor down to zoom in or out.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Zoom Out</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Zoom Out command recedes all visible data twice.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Zoom Selected</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">Zoom Selected command resets the view extents to fit all visible selected data.<p>
<p class="glsbody" style="white-space:nowrap;margin-bottom:1pt;"><b>Zoom Window</b></p>
<p class="glsbody" style="margin-top:1pt;">When this mode is enabled, hold down the left mouse button and drag the mouse todraw a rectangle. After releasing the button KUBE resets the view extents to fit the visible data inthat rectangle.<p>
<p class="glsbody"><br><br></p>

